questions.q:
The chapter describes three farm problems and the traditional answers in Vrikshayurveda. Name the Vrikshayurveda recommendation that responds to each problem:
(a) pesticide chemicals dissolving in a farm's groundwater;
(b) soil degraded by improper use of chemical fertilisers;
(c) ploughing that leaves the soil dry and without fungi, bacteria and earthworms.
(d) Name one thing Vrikshayurveda specifies for seeds.
(e) Say what the word Vrikshayurveda means, part by part.
